# Prepared ahead of A4 (git init happens only after v0.1 passes the boundary check).
/target
**/*.rs.bk

# Secrets never enter git — API keys live in .env only.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Project-local scaffold deployed by `orvena init` into a user's repo.
.orvena/

# macOS noise
.DS_Store

# Session handoffs are addressed to the next working session, not to a reader
# of this project — they say "don't touch X" and "waiting on a ruling", and
# they are false the moment the next session does anything. A slice is a
# decision record and stays true as history; a handoff is a snapshot that
# rots silently, and in a public repo the two are indistinguishable at a
# glance. They live in the private notes repo alongside their index instead.
HANDOFF_*.md
